From 8b323d280cfa716c9ffde8d3d70f8c099708689e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shota <monyuonyu@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 02:10:47 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 346/400] Assembly: a slider can be moved to a distance;
 formulas follow while a joint's panel is open

- A slider joint has "Move to a distance" (SlideDriven, SlideDistance,
  either way along the axis, a formula allowed): a valve's lift from the
  crank's angle. It was a fixed joint with a formula offset (engine field
  test 0.7.7). Solved as a fixed joint moved along its axis.
- Changing a driven joint's angle or distance in its panel recomputes the
  document, so the joints whose formulas use it (rockers, valves) follow
  at once, not at "Done".

Test: FreeCADCmd -t TestAssemblySolve

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
